Mutant: the writer that appends after the cut forgets the source system, so its next rotation writes system 0 into the new header. Must fail: a rotation after a start writes the source system, timeline and last transaction into the new header.
Apply from the repository root with git apply, and never commit it applied.

--- a/src/bin/pgcopydb/ld_spool.c
+++ b/src/bin/pgcopydb/ld_spool.c
@@ -2038,6 +2038,8 @@
 		.lastEndLSN = tail->last.endLSN,
 		.completeSize = tail->last.endOffset
 	};
+
+	writer->header.systemId = 0;
 
 	/* the cut synced the segment at that length */
 	writer->segment.size = tail->last.endOffset;
